{
  "schema_version": "fabric.model-exposure-vectors/v1",
  "rule": "Exact allowlist entries match exactly. A 'prefix*' entry (built-in or FABRIC_WIRE_MODEL_ALLOWLIST) matches when the value starts with prefix and the rest, split on [-._:/@] with empty tokens ignored, consists only of: purely numeric tokens of at most 4 digits ('numbers'); a decimal version N.N (two numeric tokens of 1-2 digits each joined by exactly '.') counted as one number; a date, either one 8-digit token matching ^20\\d{2}(0[1-9]|1[0-2])(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$ or three numeric tokens of 4, 2 and 2 digits joined by exactly '-' whose concatenation matches that pattern, which is not a number; tokens matching ^(v?\\d+[a-z]{0,2}|\\d+[a-z]\\d*|[a-z]\\d+)$ that are not purely numeric; or words of 'suffix_words' (case-sensitive). At most two numbers and at most one date (decision J2); tokens are read left to right, a date or decimal taking its tokens first. Values must also match ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:/-]{0,127}$ and contain no '://'. Anything else is exposed as 'm-' + the first 16 hex of sha256(utf-8 value).",
